LORE — hard-won lessons

File: openOODA/LORE.oot
When you solve a hard bug or find a hidden rule, add one short sentence here.
Do not repeat RULES.oot.

1. AST injection. The C AST parser cannot handle un-braced macros in comma expressions (example: OO_FLIGHT_RECORDER_LOG). If you inject a C macro, use ((void)0), not do {} while(0). Learned 2026-08-11.

2. Path-A decoys. The compiler shuffles __oo_meta_decoy_* layouts at run time. Do not assume static memory offsets in tests. Learned 2026-08-12.

3. HITL. Human-in-the-loop tests need oo_process_policy_getenv, not raw getenv. hitl_audit_open is not in the C emitter. Learned 2026-08-11.

4. Cap gating. New std crypto or net ops fail closed with process_exit(1) until an audit lands. Learned 2026-08-12.

5. AST imports. Import tokens must be IMPORT AST nodes so file boundaries stay real and item_idx increments. Learned 2026-08-12.
